rpcs3 (0.0.42+dfsg-1foundry1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Initial Foundry Linux package of RPCS3, the PlayStation 3 emulator.
  * Built from a recursive clone at the v0.0.42 superproject commit
    cd814f8c926400cf62dab7924f723e4eb7719e50. Upstream publishes no release
    assets and its plain tag archive omits all 28 vendored submodules, so
    build.sh synthesises the orig tarball itself; the superproject commit
    pins every submodule transitively via its gitlinks, so one sha256 pin
    covers the whole tree.
  * Repack (+dfsg): drop the RPCS3/ffmpeg-core submodule, whose CMakeLists
    downloads a prebuilt ffmpeg zip from a GitHub release at configure time
    and which ships prebuilt Windows import libraries; build against Ubuntu's
    ffmpeg instead (USE_SYSTEM_FFMPEG=ON). Also drop the prebuilt Windows
    OpenCV submodule (unreferenced on Linux; USE_SYSTEM_OPENCV is on), the
    llvm-project submodule (BUILD_LLVM=OFF, we link system LLVM 21), and four
    sample/test binaries vendored by VulkanMemoryAllocator, stb and
    SoundTouch. The published source package therefore contains no prebuilt
    binaries at all.
  * Build with USE_NATIVE_INSTRUCTIONS=OFF: upstream defaults it ON, which
    compiles -march=native and would produce a binary that crashes on any
    host older than the builder.
  * Patch rpcs3/git-version.cmake so the binary reports its real version.
    Upstream hardcodes "local_build" unless a .git directory is present, and
    a source package must not ship one.
  * Add a section-1 man page (Debian Policy 12.1); upstream ships none.
  * PS3 firmware (PS3UPDAT.PUP) is copyrighted Sony material: it is not
    shipped, not fetched, and not linked to. The user installs it themselves.

 -- Foundry Linux <packages@foundrylinux.org>  Wed, 05 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
